        ],
        "tcxo": true,
        "telemetry_power_mW": 10,
        "wifi_webui": true
      },
      "type": "performance"
    },
    {
      "params": {
        "note": "MCU ESP8285, RF chip Semtech SX1281, built-in TCXO. WiFi built in: firmware update and configuration via the WebUI. ELRS target 'RadioMaster RP1 2.4GHz RX' (upload via UART, WiFi, or Betaflight passthrough).",
        "source": [
          "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0609/8324/7079/files/RP1_User_Manual.pdf?v=1722923320",
          "https://radiomasterrc.com/products/rp1-expresslrs-2-4ghz-nano-receiver",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ExpressLRS/targets/master/targets.json"
        ]
      },
      "type": "usage_note"
    },
    {
      "params": {
        "note": "Binding: set a binding phrase, or power the RX on/off 3 times until the LED double-blinks (bind mode), then press [BIND] in the ExpressLRS Lua script; solid LED = bound. BOOT pad: short to GND with a metal object while powering on to enter firmware-upgrade (bootloader) mode.",
        "source": [
          "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0609/8324/7079/files/RP1_User_Manual.pdf?v=1722923320",
          "https://www.expresslrs.org/quick-start/receivers/wiring-up/"
        ]
      },
      "type": "usage_note"
    },
    {
      "params": {
        "note": "Mounting: no mounting holes. Secure with heat shrink, foam tape or zip tie after bench-testing (ELRS docs: do not shrink wrap until the receiver is tested; heat shrink can press the boot button/pad).",
        "source": [
          "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0609/8324/7079/files/RP1_User_Manual.pdf?v=1722923320",
          "https://www.expresslrs.org/quick-start/receivers/wiring-up/"
        ]
      },
      "type": "usage_note"
    },
    {
      "params": {
        "note": "Sold as FCC and LBT variants (regulatory firmware domain); hardware is the same product. Package: RP1 receiver, 65mm UFL T antenna, user manual card, 4x silicone wires (manual) / CRSF wire (product page).",
        "source": [
          "https://radiomasterrc.com/products/rp1-expresslrs-2-4ghz-nano-receiver",
          "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0609/8324/7079/files/RP1_User_Manual.pdf?v=1722923320"
        ]
      },
      "type": "usage_note"
    },
    {
      "params": {
        "field": "RF chip",
        "resolution": "SX1281 (manufacturer spec tables; chip marking '1281' in the manual drawing). SX1276 is a sub-GHz chip and a clear typo.",
        "sources": [
          "src_manual (EN) + src_product spec table",
          "src_product description + src_rdq",
